00:25:08.810 --> 00:25:09.890
transcends industry.

00:25:09.890 --> 00:25:12.350
So one of the things that
you have to think about

00:25:12.350 --> 00:25:15.630
is, the baby boomers are
retiring en masse right now.

00:25:15.630 --> 00:25:17.750
And so what you have
going on, what we

00:25:17.750 --> 00:25:19.102
call institutional memory loss.

00:25:19.102 --> 00:25:21.560
So in the instance that you
were talking about with Philips

00:25:21.560 --> 00:25:23.852
Healthcare, I actually used
to work for Philips Medical

00:25:23.852 --> 00:25:26.130
Systems, and worked
in radiology.

00:25:26.130 --> 00:25:27.630
So I know it all too well.

00:25:27.630 --> 00:25:30.170
So what happens-- and it
happens in every line of work--

00:25:30.170 --> 00:25:35.943
you have people that retire, get
fired, leave, whatever it is.

00:25:35.943 --> 00:25:37.610
And what they do is,
they take with them

00:25:37.610 --> 00:25:40.068
all that knowledge that they
built up over the years that's

00:25:40.068 --> 00:25:41.420
institutional knowledge.

00:25:41.420 --> 00:25:44.130
And what happens is,
there's a giant vacuum.

00:25:44.130 --> 00:25:44.930
There's a gap.

00:25:44.930 --> 00:25:46.900
So something like
Enterprise Search

00:25:46.900 --> 00:25:49.010
helps address that by
getting everything,

00:25:49.010 --> 00:25:51.980
all that information, all
that data, on the cloud

00:25:51.980 --> 00:25:53.843
so people can readily find it.

00:25:53.843 --> 00:25:56.510
Otherwise, you have situations--
and I've been in this situation

00:25:56.510 --> 00:25:59.210
