social responsibility.

00:29:32.430 --> 00:29:34.745
Tim Needles is our CEO
and really lives it.

00:29:34.745 --> 00:29:36.620
I almost jumped an
announcement that we have,

00:29:36.620 --> 00:29:39.140
something-- but we do a
lot with the homeless.

00:29:39.140 --> 00:29:40.385
And in terms of--

00:29:40.385 --> 00:29:41.510
JOSE PAGAN: Oh, I remember.

00:29:41.510 --> 00:29:42.170
BRYAN KOKISH: Yeah.

00:29:42.170 --> 00:29:43.170
JOSE PAGAN: Yeah,
we have a nonprofit

00:29:43.170 --> 00:29:44.750
that him and his
wife created called

00:29:44.750 --> 00:29:47.180
Onix Outreach that
helps fight hunger

00:29:47.180 --> 00:29:48.700
and homelessness in Cleveland.

00:29:48.700 --> 00:29:49.370
AJA HAMMERLY: Oh, awesome.

00:29:49.370 --> 00:29:50.360
JOSE PAGAN: Oh, it's fantastic.

00:29:50.360 --> 00:29:51.527
Yeah, check out the website.

00:29:51.527 --> 00:29:53.610
And for them to
give back like that

00:29:53.610 --> 00:29:56.150
is a direct relation on
who they are as people.

00:29:56.150 --> 00:29:58.130
I mean, we are fascinating
people to work with.

00:29:58.130 --> 00:29:59.810
BRYAN KOKISH: And the thing
is, the whole company's

00:29:59.810 --> 00:30:00.530
involved in that.

00:30:00.530 --> 00:30:02.670
It's actually
written into our HR.

00:30:02.670 --> 00:30:04.090
What do we get, a day?

00:30:04.090 --> 00:30:05.260
JOSE PAGAN: We get one
furlough day a year

00:30:05.260 --> 00:30:05.820
to do [INAUDIBLE]
nonprofit work.

00:30:05.820 --> 00:30:07.070
BRYAN KOKISH: To
do volunteer work.

00:30:07.070 --> 00:30:07.940
AJA HAMMERLY: That's awesome.

00:30:07.940 --> 00:30:09.500
JOSE PAGAN: And then throughout
the rest of the year,

00:30:09.500 --> 00:30:10.590
everybody helps out with--

00:30:10.590 --> 00:30:12.298
I mean, every year
around Christmas time,

00:30:12.298 --> 00:30:14.068
we do a clothing and food drive.

00:30:14.068 --> 00:30:15.610
I mean, we work with
some of the most

00:30:15.610 --> 00:30:18.890
